.TH OPJ_JP3D_COMPRESS 1 "2026-02-21" "OpenJP3D 0.1.0" "OpenJP3D Manual"
.SH NAME
opj_jp3d_compress \- encode a raw binary volume into a JP3D codestream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opj_jp3d_compress
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB \-i\ \fIinput.raw\fR
.RB \-o\ \fIoutput.jp3d\fR
.RB \-W\ \fIwidth\fR
.RB \-H\ \fIheight\fR
.RB \-D\ \fIdepth\fR
.RB [ \-p\ \fIprec\fR ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-c\ \fInumcomps\fR ]
.RB [ \-t\ \fItw,th,td\fR ]
.RB [ \-n\ \fIrx,ry,rz\fR ]
.RB [ \-r\ \fIrate\fR ]
.RB [ \-f\ \fI53|97\fR ]
.RB [ \-H2K ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opj_jp3d_compress
reads a raw binary volume file and encodes it into a JP3D (JPEG\ 2000
Part\ 10) codestream. The input file must contain sample data in
z\-major order, little-endian.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i\ \fIfile\fR
Input raw binary volume file (required).
.TP
.BR \-o\ \fIfile\fR
Output JP3D codestream file (required).
.TP
.BR \-W\ \fIw\fR
Volume width in X samples (required).
.TP
.BR \-H\ \fIh\fR
Volume height in Y samples (required).
.TP
.BR \-D\ \fId\fR
Volume depth in Z slices (required).
.TP
.BR \-p\ \fIprec\fR
Bit depth per sample (default: 8).
.TP
.BR \-s
Treat samples as signed (default: unsigned).
.TP
.BR \-c\ \fInumcomps\fR
Number of components (default: 1).
.TP
.BR \-t\ \fItw,th,td\fR
Tile dimensions (default: whole volume).
.TP
.BR \-n\ \fIrx,ry,rz\fR
DWT decomposition levels per axis (default: 3,3,3).
.TP
.BR \-r\ \fIrate\fR
Target bits/sample; 0 means lossless (default: 0).
.TP
.BR \-f\ \fI53|97\fR
DWT filter: 53 (lossless 5/3) or 97 (lossy 9/7). Default: 53.
.TP
.BR \-H2K
Enable HTJ2K high\-throughput block coder.
.TP
.BR \-v
Verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-h ,\ \-\-help
Print help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
opj_jp3d_compress \-i volume.raw \-o volume.jp3d \-W 256 \-H 256 \-D 128 \-p 16
opj_jp3d_compress \-i vol.raw \-o vol.jp3d \-W 64 \-H 64 \-D 64 \-H2K
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR opj_jp3d_decompress (1),
.BR opj_jp3d_dump (1),
.BR opj_jp3d_transcode (1)
